l":"https://api.github.com/users/GentlemanHal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GentlemanHal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GentlemanHal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GentlemanHal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GentlemanHal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GentlemanHal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GentlemanHal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GentlemanHal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GentlemanHal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T22:23:31Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T23:01:59Z","body":"I also noticed `coreaudiod` using ~10% CPU constantly. This is true even if Godot is inactive on another desktop, which for reference reduces Godots CPU usage to ~1.5%.\n\nI checked Chrome playing some music and `coreaudiod` uses ~8% CPU, which drops back to 0 when the music is stopped, even if Chrome is still otherwise active on the same desktop.\n\nObviously this isn't an exhaustive test, but it does feel like Godot is causing excessive CPU usage in `coreaudiod`\n\nOn my machine `corespeechd` isn't using any CPU.\n\n### Tested versions\nv4.7.2.stable.official [ed1daf0bf] (I did also notice this on previous versions)\n\n### System information\nApple M2 Pro Tahoe 26.6.2\n\nEdit: I assume this is a duplicate of this older issue https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/38154, which seems to already have a PR 🎉 ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5334805969/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]